# The Voynich Manuscript — An English Rendering

> **{{ banner }}**

Rendered under hypothesis **{{ hypothesis.id }}** (`{{ hypothesis.variant }}`). Run against a
control corpus built to encode nothing at all, the same pipeline produced *more* confident
English than it does from the manuscript — 75.1% of words against 61.1%. Four of the five
failure tests agreed in advance were met, and the decipherment attempt is **declared
unsuccessful**. Treat every word below as machine output, never as the meaning of a Voynich
word.

## How to read this file

- One section per page, in manuscript order; {{ page_count }} pages carry text.
- Each page header gives its section, Currier language, scribal hand, quire, line count, and
  the share of its words that survived the confidence gate.
- **Illustration:** names what is drawn on the leaf. No images are included here.
- `[…]` marks one word the pipeline could not read, `[…×3]` three consecutive ones. Unread
  words at the start
  and end of a block are dropped rather than marked.
- Paragraph blocks come from the IVTFF `<%>`/`<$>` markers. **Label:** lines are captions
  written beside an illustration, not running prose — they are the least reliable text here
  (21% gated coverage against 61% for paragraphs).
- Punctuation and sentence boundaries do not exist in the source and none have been invented.

